<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέτερ-ος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽ ἕτερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδάτερος</span></b>  (q.v.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>neither of the two</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.118
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				470a
			</span></i>, etc.; also divisim, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μηδὲ μεθ᾽ ἑτέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.67
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				72
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲ καθ᾽ ἕτερα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.59
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδετέρως</span>
			<i>in neither way</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1460b35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἔχοντες</span>
			<i>being indifferent</i> (neither friends nor foes), ib.<i><span class="en">
				1453b19
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
